        "original_id": "f96b7a29-e3c8-5559-b42d-188161d2fa2a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee, North Carolina; Swain County, North Carolina; Graham County, North Carolina; Cherokee County, North Carolina\n- Dams: Hiwassee Dam; Fontana Dam\n- Organizations: Tennessee Valley Authority\n- Rivers and Reservoirs: Little Tennessee River; Hiwassee River; Hiwassee Reservoir\n\nFacts:\n- Fontana Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States.\n- Hiwassee is a small village in Cherokee County, North Carolina, located next to Hiwassee Dam and the artificial Hiwassee Reservoir on the Hiwassee River.\n- Hiwassee Dam is 307 feet tall.\n- Hiwassee Dam is the third highest dam in the Tennessee Valley Authority system, behind Fontana Dam and Watauga Dam.",
